WEBVTT

00:00:08.410 --> 00:00:08.660
"Minagi"

00:00:08.660 --> 00:00:09.910
"Minagi"
Over here!

00:00:09.910 --> 00:00:10.750
"Minagi"
Wait!

00:00:10.750 --> 00:00:11.410
"Minagi"
Not giving it back!

00:00:11.410 --> 00:00:12.410
Not giving it back!

00:00:12.410 --> 00:00:14.120
Meanie!

00:00:16.410 --> 00:00:20.200
Ataru and Takeru, no running in the house!

00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:21.750
'Kay...

00:00:21.750 --> 00:00:22.950
Don't make trouble for Kaoru.

00:00:22.950 --> 00:00:24.160
"Tsuzuru"
Don't make trouble for Kaoru.

00:00:24.160 --> 00:00:25.160
"Tsuzuru"
Fine...

00:00:25.160 --> 00:00:27.700
--One, two, one, two!
--Kaoru!

00:00:27.700 --> 00:00:29.950
Dad's phone's ringing.

00:00:29.950 --> 00:00:31.830
It's Tsuzuru.

00:00:33.080 --> 00:00:36.830
Dad? Oh, hey, Kaoru.

00:00:36.830 --> 00:00:38.790
Nah, it's okay.

00:00:38.790 --> 00:00:43.040
Just calling to tell Dad that I found
a theater troupe with a dorm.

00:00:43.040 --> 00:00:44.830
You'll take care of everybody?

00:00:44.830 --> 00:00:47.830
Don't worry about things here.
Get out there to chase your dream.

00:00:47.830 --> 00:00:51.540
"A Midsummer Night's Dream"
"The Merchant of Venice" "Julius Caesar"
Don't worry about things here.
Get out there to chase your dream.

00:00:51.540 --> 00:00:55.080
Thanks. Catch you later.

00:02:35.120 --> 00:02:36.870
"Romeo and Julius"

00:02:36.870 --> 00:02:38.750
"Romeo and Julius"
Director, please use this room.
It's the room Yukio used.

00:02:38.750 --> 00:02:42.450
Director, please use this room.
It's the room Yukio used.

00:02:42.450 --> 00:02:44.160
Dad's room?

00:02:52.950 --> 00:02:54.790
I'll stay here, too.

00:02:54.790 --> 00:02:56.330
Absolutely not.

00:02:56.330 --> 00:02:59.660
You're still a high schooler, Masumi.

00:02:59.660 --> 00:03:02.870
We need parental permission
for you to stay in the dorm.

00:03:02.870 --> 00:03:04.040
It's fine.

00:03:04.040 --> 00:03:05.790
It is <i>not </i>fine.

00:03:05.790 --> 00:03:09.080
I'll also introduce myself to your parents.
What's their number?

00:03:09.080 --> 00:03:13.080
You already want to meet my parents?
We just started dating...

00:03:13.080 --> 00:03:15.700
We aren't dating.

00:03:15.700 --> 00:03:19.250
They're busy and there's a time difference,
so probably can't get a hold of them.

00:03:19.250 --> 00:03:21.200
Time difference? They're overseas?

00:03:21.200 --> 00:03:23.540
Where'd they go this time?

00:03:24.540 --> 00:03:26.000
I forget.

00:03:27.410 --> 00:03:32.000
I left a message, but you should
go home for today.

00:03:32.000 --> 00:03:37.910
Let him stay. It's late, plus I prepared
enough food for him.

00:03:37.910 --> 00:03:41.160
Oh, all right. About room assignments...

00:03:41.160 --> 00:03:44.290
Don't care where if I'm not in your room.

00:03:44.290 --> 00:03:47.120
I don't mind rooming with Masumi.

00:03:47.120 --> 00:03:49.040
I'm good with anything.

00:03:51.250 --> 00:03:53.580
Looks like we're roommates.

00:03:53.580 --> 00:03:56.000
We'll all be living the dorm life together, huh.

00:03:56.000 --> 00:03:59.290
Sakuya, you already got
parental permission to stay, right?

00:03:59.290 --> 00:04:01.870
Uh... Not really...

00:04:01.870 --> 00:04:03.120
You haven't told them?!

00:04:03.120 --> 00:04:03.950
Not yet.

00:04:03.950 --> 00:04:05.540
You haven't?!

00:04:05.540 --> 00:04:07.700
Will you shush!

00:04:11.330 --> 00:04:13.120
Yoshinaga speaking.

00:04:13.120 --> 00:04:15.250
--Huh?
--Hello?

00:04:15.250 --> 00:04:18.620
U-Um, is this the residence of Sakuya Sakuma?

00:04:18.620 --> 00:04:20.330
It is.

00:04:20.330 --> 00:04:24.830
Apologies for calling so late. I'm from
the theater troupe, Mankai Company--

00:04:24.830 --> 00:04:27.120
Theater troupe, you say?

00:04:29.040 --> 00:04:32.700
...that's the situation. Do you give permission?

00:04:32.700 --> 00:04:34.910
Does it costs money?

00:04:34.910 --> 00:04:36.080
It doesn't.

00:04:36.080 --> 00:04:38.370
If that's the case, then by all means.

00:04:38.370 --> 00:04:43.580
Just make sure to send him to school.
It'd cause trouble for us otherwise.

00:04:44.620 --> 00:04:48.040
She gave permission, so you're all set.

00:04:48.040 --> 00:04:50.540
Thank you, ma'am.

00:04:50.540 --> 00:04:57.000
My parents passed away when I was young,
so I've stayed with relatives since.

00:04:57.000 --> 00:04:59.250
That's why our last names don't match.

00:04:59.250 --> 00:05:01.120
So that's why.

00:05:01.120 --> 00:05:04.700
I'm excited! It's my first time
ever having my own room!

00:05:04.700 --> 00:05:07.830
I'll work hard as a troupe member!

00:05:07.830 --> 00:05:12.370
You better! Or else this dorm'll
be shut down, too.

00:05:12.370 --> 00:05:14.120
I don't want that!

00:05:14.120 --> 00:05:18.200
Everybody! Our feast is ready!

00:05:20.000 --> 00:05:21.910
Eat up!

00:05:21.910 --> 00:05:23.370
What the...

00:05:23.370 --> 00:05:25.790
Food porn? Someone censor this.

00:05:25.790 --> 00:05:27.870
You should've seen yesterday's.

00:05:27.870 --> 00:05:31.250
Don't hold back. There's plenty more!

00:05:31.250 --> 00:05:34.040
Guess I'll try a bite.

00:05:34.040 --> 00:05:35.830
Be careful!

00:05:38.910 --> 00:05:40.790
I-I give up.

00:05:40.790 --> 00:05:42.700
Tsuzuru!

00:05:44.290 --> 00:05:45.660
I'm done.

00:05:45.660 --> 00:05:49.000
Wait, you didn't even touch it!

00:05:49.000 --> 00:05:50.500
Not hungry anymore.

00:05:50.500 --> 00:05:54.120
Don't hold back. There's enough for seconds!

00:05:54.120 --> 00:05:57.660
I'll make some curry!

00:05:57.660 --> 00:05:59.120
Huh?

00:06:01.080 --> 00:06:03.120
Wow!

00:06:06.040 --> 00:06:07.790
It's delicious!

00:06:07.790 --> 00:06:10.120
I could eat your cooking forever.

00:06:10.120 --> 00:06:12.450
What curry roux did you use?

00:06:12.450 --> 00:06:17.120
Roux? You mean the store-bought stuff?

00:06:17.120 --> 00:06:19.790
I'd never use that crap.

00:06:19.790 --> 00:06:23.200
A heresy that leads to idleness!
That stuff's a blasphemy against all curry!

00:06:23.200 --> 00:06:26.040
It is? Then what did you use?

00:06:26.040 --> 00:06:29.910
I'm glad you asked!
To start, this spice is a must--

00:06:29.910 --> 00:06:31.080
Thanks, I'm done.

00:06:31.080 --> 00:06:32.370
It was great.

00:06:32.370 --> 00:06:33.700
I'll grab seconds.

00:06:33.700 --> 00:06:35.370
Listen to me!

00:06:35.370 --> 00:06:38.950
This was the best curry I've ever had.

00:06:38.950 --> 00:06:42.250
Really? I'm happy to make it year round.

00:06:42.250 --> 00:06:44.950
Please don't.

00:06:50.620 --> 00:06:52.910
What are these?

00:06:52.910 --> 00:06:57.620
The original Spring Troupe's materials.
I thought they'd help give you some ideas.

00:06:59.540 --> 00:06:59.750
These are legit.

00:06:59.750 --> 00:07:01.370
"Romeo and Juliet" "The Stage Is a Dream"
These are legit.

00:07:01.370 --> 00:07:03.500
"Romeo and Juliet" "The Stage Is a Dream"
The original Spring Troupe tended to put on
lighthearted, more conventional plays,

00:07:03.500 --> 00:07:05.290
The original Spring Troupe tended to put on
lighthearted, more conventional plays,

00:07:05.290 --> 00:07:07.200
so they were the most popular.

00:07:08.580 --> 00:07:11.660
These were from the original Spring Troupe?

00:07:15.370 --> 00:07:19.290
Today we're going out to get more members.

00:07:19.290 --> 00:07:20.620
More members?

00:07:20.620 --> 00:07:23.540
The original Spring Troupe was a group of five,

00:07:23.540 --> 00:07:27.040
so we'd probably need at least
that many to fill out our cast.

00:07:27.040 --> 00:07:30.620
Let's go do some street acts.
They'll be good practice, too.

00:07:30.620 --> 00:07:32.290
--Yes, ma'am!
--'Kay!

00:07:32.290 --> 00:07:34.040
Wake up already.

00:07:35.370 --> 00:07:39.290
I have a home now, thanks to Mankai Company!

00:07:39.290 --> 00:07:43.250
Now, I can have warm meals
every day! Right, bro?

00:07:43.250 --> 00:07:45.830
No more sleeping in the doghouse.

00:07:45.830 --> 00:07:47.750
D-Doghouse?!

00:07:47.750 --> 00:07:48.660
What the?

00:07:48.660 --> 00:07:49.750
Ugh.

00:07:49.750 --> 00:07:51.200
So cringe.

00:07:51.200 --> 00:07:53.040
Talk about hammy acting.

00:07:53.040 --> 00:07:55.250
Well, we're drawing attention at least...

00:07:55.250 --> 00:07:59.290
I see, so these are Japanese hams?

00:07:59.290 --> 00:08:04.540
Bake it or put it in stew. Fresh hams, they are!

00:08:04.540 --> 00:08:06.700
Stop calling them hams!

00:08:06.700 --> 00:08:09.700
Oh, sorry. I beg your pardon, lady.

00:08:09.700 --> 00:08:11.660
Who's the guy in the mask?

00:08:11.660 --> 00:08:13.450
A movie star?

00:08:13.450 --> 00:08:16.120
We're drawing more attention <i>here</i>.

00:08:16.120 --> 00:08:20.620
If you're an actor from another troupe,
would you mind going elsewhere--

00:08:20.620 --> 00:08:23.620
I'm no actor.

00:08:23.620 --> 00:08:26.250
Just a foreigner passing through!

00:08:26.250 --> 00:08:28.500
What's going on?

00:08:28.500 --> 00:08:30.620
Is he promoting a show?

00:08:30.620 --> 00:08:32.410
He says he's not an actor.

00:08:32.410 --> 00:08:34.580
I've never seen clothes like that.

00:08:34.580 --> 00:08:37.200
This is what my countrymen wear.

00:08:37.200 --> 00:08:40.330
You're a foreigner? Are you sightseeing?

00:08:40.330 --> 00:08:46.700
I'm studying abroad. I've always wanted
to learn about the city of theater.

00:08:46.700 --> 00:08:50.620
Would you like to join our theater troupe,
Mankai Company?

00:08:50.620 --> 00:08:54.830
We have a dorm, so you'd have a place to stay.
And you can study theater!

00:08:54.830 --> 00:08:55.830
You serious?

00:08:55.830 --> 00:08:57.790
You'll take just about anyone, huh.

00:08:57.790 --> 00:08:59.450
Can you even say your lines?!

00:08:59.450 --> 00:09:00.620
Not a problemo!

00:09:00.620 --> 00:09:02.000
I'm not convinced!

00:09:02.000 --> 00:09:04.790
I'll join your Manzai Company!

00:09:04.790 --> 00:09:06.540
It's <i>Mankai</i>!

00:09:09.000 --> 00:09:11.750
I'm Citron. Nice to meet you.

00:09:11.750 --> 00:09:13.620
Same here.

00:09:15.750 --> 00:09:17.830
Let's call it a day.

00:09:17.830 --> 00:09:19.540
I can still keep going!

00:09:19.540 --> 00:09:23.620
Staying out here longer won't do us any good.

00:09:23.620 --> 00:09:25.790
That's right, Sakuya.

00:09:27.330 --> 00:09:29.950
They say that slow and steady spins the race.

00:09:29.950 --> 00:09:32.040
C-Citron?!

00:09:32.040 --> 00:09:35.330
You mean "slow and steady wins the... race"?

00:09:38.870 --> 00:09:43.080
--I'll spin you more exuberantly than usual!
--Citron! Please stop... spinning me... around!

00:09:43.080 --> 00:09:44.500
As you wish!

00:09:45.620 --> 00:09:47.950
My head's spinning...

00:09:47.950 --> 00:09:48.790
Oh?

00:09:48.790 --> 00:09:50.580
I-I'm sorry!

00:09:50.580 --> 00:09:51.870
Are you okay?

00:09:51.870 --> 00:09:52.910
Yes.

00:09:52.910 --> 00:09:56.290
Sorry. Sakuya's mistake is my mistake.

00:09:56.290 --> 00:09:57.910
Don't worry about it.

00:09:57.910 --> 00:10:02.950
Excuse me, but are you looking
for housing around here?

00:10:04.040 --> 00:10:06.290
In fact, I am.

00:10:07.330 --> 00:10:08.540
"Veludo Housing Finder"

00:10:08.540 --> 00:10:10.580
"Veludo Housing Finder"
You have your own dorm?

00:10:10.580 --> 00:10:13.040
Room and board are included.

00:10:13.040 --> 00:10:20.830
It's tempting, but two to a room
might be difficult. I've accumulated a lot.

00:10:20.830 --> 00:10:24.790
You can get a room to yourself
if I room with Citron!

00:10:24.790 --> 00:10:27.450
I'm okay with that!

00:10:27.450 --> 00:10:31.290
If that's the case,
I'd like to hear more about it.

00:10:32.290 --> 00:10:38.200
First a foreigner and now a salaryman?
I should get a job.

00:10:38.200 --> 00:10:44.250
I'd like to happily announce that Itaru
Chigasaki and Citron have joined the troupe!

00:10:44.250 --> 00:10:46.250
Glad to have you.

00:10:46.250 --> 00:10:51.580
Splendid! You've gathered a full
team of five. I knew you could do it!

00:10:51.580 --> 00:10:53.200
Where's Itaru, then?

00:10:53.200 --> 00:10:55.580
He already went home to prepare to move in.

00:10:55.580 --> 00:11:00.660
We should get started on deciding
what we'll do for our performance.

00:11:00.660 --> 00:11:03.540
Itaru's not here, though. Is that okay?

00:11:03.540 --> 00:11:04.870
We're on a tight schedule.

00:11:04.870 --> 00:11:08.250
We won't make it unless we start
prepping our script right away.

00:11:08.250 --> 00:11:11.750
How about reusing one of the
original Spring Troupe's scripts?

00:11:11.750 --> 00:11:13.290
That might be good...

00:11:13.290 --> 00:11:14.660
Um...

00:11:16.660 --> 00:11:19.540
Can I write the script?

00:11:19.540 --> 00:11:21.580
I remember you mentioning...

00:11:21.580 --> 00:11:23.620
You want to be a playwright, huh.

00:11:23.620 --> 00:11:28.200
I understand why you're asking,
but with the amount of rehearsal we have...

00:11:28.200 --> 00:11:30.750
How about you write for our next show?

00:11:30.750 --> 00:11:34.080
Are you sure we'll have another show?

00:11:34.080 --> 00:11:39.580
Tsuzuru, how long would it
take you to write the script?

00:11:41.410 --> 00:11:43.540
One week.

00:11:43.540 --> 00:11:45.910
Can I have one week to give it a shot?

00:11:45.910 --> 00:11:49.830
One week?! That's impossible, even for pros!

00:11:49.830 --> 00:11:51.620
--Sure.
--Director?!

00:11:51.620 --> 00:11:52.830
You'll let me?

00:11:52.830 --> 00:11:58.870
I'll let you off rehearsal for a week.
But you <i>have </i>to finish the script.

00:11:58.870 --> 00:12:02.950
And it better be good.
Otherwise be ready for my wrath.

00:12:02.950 --> 00:12:04.200
Scary.

00:12:04.200 --> 00:12:06.660
This troupe's survival is on the line.

00:12:06.660 --> 00:12:11.540
Don't let it go under just because
you wanted to write the script.

00:12:11.540 --> 00:12:12.870
'Kay!

00:12:16.700 --> 00:12:19.370
Have you decided on what to write about?

00:12:19.370 --> 00:12:21.620
After looking through the original
Spring Troupe's materials,

00:12:21.620 --> 00:12:27.080
Romeo and Juliet keep popping
into mind. I plan to go with that.

00:12:27.080 --> 00:12:29.410
Who will play Juliet?

00:12:29.410 --> 00:12:33.290
Cross-dressing doesn't seem like
an option for this group.

00:12:33.290 --> 00:12:36.370
I'll make it work. Trust me.

00:12:38.910 --> 00:12:42.950
Do you think we can count on him?

00:12:42.950 --> 00:12:48.250
We could do a read-through of the original
Spring Troupe's script just in case.

00:12:48.250 --> 00:12:52.950
It's okay. Let's trust him.

00:12:52.950 --> 00:12:55.120
"Move-It-All Movers"

00:12:55.450 --> 00:13:00.160
Itaru and Citron will be joining
our rehearsals from now.

00:13:00.160 --> 00:13:04.250
I might hold you back since I have
no experience, but thanks for having me.

00:13:04.250 --> 00:13:05.620
Thanks for having me!

00:13:05.620 --> 00:13:08.200
Let's get started then.

00:13:09.120 --> 00:13:14.080
Dad! Er... What time are you coming home today?

00:13:14.080 --> 00:13:16.410
I might be home late today again.

00:13:16.410 --> 00:13:18.200
--Again? You promised you'd come home earlier!

00:13:18.200 --> 00:13:21.000
--Sakuya's acting is a little heavy-handed.
--Again? You promised you'd come home earlier!

00:13:21.000 --> 00:13:22.370
--Sakuya's acting is a little heavy-handed.
--Dad, it's your fault Mom left!

00:13:22.370 --> 00:13:24.250
--Masumi's acting is faultless.
--Dad, it's your fault Mom left!

00:13:24.250 --> 00:13:25.500
Bro?!

00:13:25.500 --> 00:13:26.450
Let go.

00:13:26.450 --> 00:13:28.580
Stop it.

00:13:28.580 --> 00:13:32.250
--Citron and Itaru could work on some things,
but they pass as beginners.

00:13:32.250 --> 00:13:34.830
--My blood's bursting!
--Citron and Itaru could work on some things,
but they pass as beginners.

00:13:34.830 --> 00:13:35.580
--Calm down!
--Citron and Itaru could work on some things,
but they pass as beginners.

00:13:35.580 --> 00:13:36.660
--Calm down!
--They'll do so much more with experience!

00:13:36.660 --> 00:13:40.540
--They'll do so much more with experience!

00:13:41.500 --> 00:13:43.250
Okay, next we'll--

00:13:49.580 --> 00:13:51.910
Rehearsal's until 9:00, right?

00:13:51.910 --> 00:13:54.830
Oh, sorry. It's already time.

00:13:54.830 --> 00:13:56.790
I can keep going!

00:13:56.790 --> 00:13:59.500
I can go until morning if you're here.

00:13:59.500 --> 00:14:04.660
We shouldn't overdo things.
I have work tomorrow, too.

00:14:04.660 --> 00:14:08.790
That's true. Let's call it a day.

00:14:08.790 --> 00:14:12.660
Um, is it okay if I practice a little more?

00:14:12.660 --> 00:14:14.950
I'll stay, too.

00:14:14.950 --> 00:14:17.250
Oh, all right. But only 30 more minutes.

00:14:17.250 --> 00:14:19.080
Yes, ma'am!

00:14:19.080 --> 00:14:22.120
I'm going back. Good work, everyone.

00:15:00.080 --> 00:15:01.540
Citron?

00:15:01.540 --> 00:15:05.660
We have the same idea.
Here to seize the script, right?

00:15:05.660 --> 00:15:08.540
Citron?! No, of course not!

00:15:08.540 --> 00:15:14.120
He's been cooped up in his room,
even during meal times. I'm worried.

00:15:14.120 --> 00:15:17.910
True... like a cooped chicken.

00:15:17.910 --> 00:15:19.580
Well...

00:15:21.290 --> 00:15:23.660
...rather than worry, open sesame!

00:15:23.660 --> 00:15:24.660
Wait!

00:15:24.660 --> 00:15:29.370
Citron, we can't just go in!

00:15:48.410 --> 00:15:50.580
I fell asleep...

00:16:00.700 --> 00:16:04.950
"Tsuzuru, we can't wait to see your script!"
"Tsuzuru, ewe can dew it!"

00:16:07.540 --> 00:16:11.580
You mean "you can do it," right?

00:16:11.580 --> 00:16:12.580
"New Message"

00:16:17.700 --> 00:16:18.540
"Bro, how's it going?"
"Don't fall asleep at your desk again."

00:16:18.540 --> 00:16:20.870
"Bro, how's it going?"
"Don't fall asleep at your desk again."
Kaoru knows me too well.

00:16:20.870 --> 00:16:22.450
"Bro, how's it going?"
"Don't fall asleep at your desk again."

00:16:25.200 --> 00:16:27.200
That's bitter.

00:16:36.200 --> 00:16:37.500
Here goes!

00:16:44.120 --> 00:16:48.410
It's been one week. How has Tsuzuru been?

00:16:48.410 --> 00:16:49.950
Dunno.

00:16:49.950 --> 00:16:51.620
He's in the room, right?

00:16:51.620 --> 00:16:53.250
--Probably.
--Probably?!

00:16:53.250 --> 00:16:56.200
You're roommates. You don't talk?

00:16:56.200 --> 00:16:57.450
Nope.

00:16:57.450 --> 00:17:02.620
He hasn't been going to class either.
It might be good to check up on him.

00:17:03.540 --> 00:17:05.540
I'll go see how he's doing.

00:17:05.540 --> 00:17:09.540
What will we do if he doesn't
finish writing the script?

00:17:09.540 --> 00:17:14.580
We use a different one. I know it sounds harsh,
but we can't wait any longer.

00:17:14.580 --> 00:17:16.790
I'm sure Tsuzuru'll finish.

00:17:16.790 --> 00:17:20.200
Yes, I think so, too!

00:17:20.200 --> 00:17:23.500
I'll be back. It's my job as the director to go.

00:17:23.500 --> 00:17:25.250
I go if you go.

00:17:25.250 --> 00:17:26.750
Oh! Me, too!

00:17:26.750 --> 00:17:31.450
Sorry, but I think I'll go back to my room.

00:17:31.450 --> 00:17:35.750
I don't feel well. I just need to rest a little.

00:17:35.750 --> 00:17:39.290
Okay, hope you feel better.

00:17:40.910 --> 00:17:43.160
Tsuzuru, are you there?

00:17:44.450 --> 00:17:46.450
Maybe he died.

00:17:46.450 --> 00:17:48.290
Tsuzuru! I'm coming in!

00:17:50.000 --> 00:17:52.000
Tsuzuru!

00:17:52.000 --> 00:17:53.120
What's wrong?

00:17:53.120 --> 00:17:54.910
Oh no! Call an ambulance!

00:17:54.910 --> 00:17:56.870
--Oh, Tsuzuru! How could you die?

00:17:56.870 --> 00:17:59.750
--Tsuzuru, wake up! What's wrong?
--Oh, Tsuzuru! How could you die?

00:17:59.750 --> 00:18:00.660
Tsuzuru!

00:18:00.660 --> 00:18:02.080
Look there.

00:18:11.500 --> 00:18:14.580
"- <i>Romeo and Julius</i>. Curtain. -"
"Did it!!"

00:18:14.580 --> 00:18:16.330
"- <i>Romeo and Julius</i>. Curtain. -"
"Did it!!"
"Did it"?

00:18:16.330 --> 00:18:18.290
Does that mean...

00:18:20.750 --> 00:18:23.250
...you finished writing the script, Tsuzuru?

00:18:23.250 --> 00:18:26.910
Shh... He's just sleeping.

00:18:29.000 --> 00:18:31.500
"- <i>Romeo and Julius</i>. Curtain. -"
"Did it!!"

00:18:33.160 --> 00:18:35.370
You actually finished.

00:18:35.370 --> 00:18:39.580
Pokey-poke-poke. Tsuzuru, wake up.

00:18:39.580 --> 00:18:44.120
Let him sleep. He must not
have slept to get it finished.

00:18:44.120 --> 00:18:46.200
Oh, that's true.

00:18:46.200 --> 00:18:48.950
He has big bears under the eyes.

00:18:55.330 --> 00:18:58.500
So he turned Juliet into a boy.

00:18:58.500 --> 00:19:02.290
Yeah, but he didn't just change the gender.

00:19:02.290 --> 00:19:04.750
He made the story into one
of friendship to make it fit.

00:19:04.750 --> 00:19:06.000
I like it.

00:19:06.000 --> 00:19:08.700
I guess it's not bad.

00:19:13.250 --> 00:19:15.450
Director, the script!

00:19:15.450 --> 00:19:16.950
Tsuzuru!

00:19:17.910 --> 00:19:20.620
What'd you think... of the script?

00:19:21.620 --> 00:19:23.160
It's...

00:19:27.750 --> 00:19:30.290
It's good. It's perfect!

00:19:30.290 --> 00:19:33.160
We'll use this for our show next month!

00:19:38.620 --> 00:19:42.620
Yes!

00:19:42.620 --> 00:19:45.330
--All right!
--That's great.

00:19:45.330 --> 00:19:47.450
Phew...

00:19:48.370 --> 00:19:53.040
Oh yeah, I precast everyone before writing.

00:19:53.040 --> 00:19:55.540
Sakuya will be Romeo, the lead.

00:19:55.540 --> 00:19:57.330
Who, me?!

00:19:57.330 --> 00:20:01.330
You joined the troupe first and are the
closest fit to the Spring Troupe's image.

00:20:01.330 --> 00:20:04.790
I agree that you're always
cheerful, lively, and sincere.

00:20:04.790 --> 00:20:08.750
It's too much! I'm happy to be in
the background if I can be on stage!

00:20:08.750 --> 00:20:10.040
In the background?

00:20:10.040 --> 00:20:14.040
I mean... Is everyone all right with me--

00:20:14.040 --> 00:20:15.500
It's no protein.

00:20:15.500 --> 00:20:17.950
"No problem," right?

00:20:17.950 --> 00:20:19.790
You have trouble with sayings
in other languages, too?

00:20:19.790 --> 00:20:21.580
I don't really care.

00:20:21.580 --> 00:20:25.910
Then, it's set! You'll be the Spring Troupe's
leader and have the lead role.

00:20:25.910 --> 00:20:27.290
I'll do my best!

00:20:27.290 --> 00:20:29.040
That's the spirit!

00:20:29.040 --> 00:20:31.870
And Masumi is Julius.

00:20:33.040 --> 00:20:38.950
I'm Mercutio, Romeo's friend.
Itaru is Romeo's cousin, Tybalt.

00:20:38.950 --> 00:20:41.330
And Citron is Friar Laurence.

00:20:41.330 --> 00:20:44.080
Aw, the friar has so few lines.

00:20:44.080 --> 00:20:45.540
It's on purpose.

00:20:45.540 --> 00:20:51.200
The characters fit everyone perfectly.
You just need to perform at your best!

00:20:51.200 --> 00:20:52.950
I'm so excited!

00:20:52.950 --> 00:20:55.410
You're kinda worked up.

00:20:55.410 --> 00:20:59.830
That's 'cause we have such a great script.

00:20:59.830 --> 00:21:01.700
I can easily write a script, too.

00:21:01.700 --> 00:21:04.790
<i>You </i>put your energy into acting.

00:21:05.870 --> 00:21:10.080
We'll finally get to do a read-through
tomorrow. Give it your best!

00:21:10.080 --> 00:21:11.580
Okay!

00:21:18.290 --> 00:21:20.580
Itaru, are you there?

00:21:34.160 --> 00:21:37.250
I brought the script...

00:21:38.620 --> 00:21:40.080
Get the hell out!

00:21:40.080 --> 00:21:45.250
Argh, goddammit! That cost me three kills!

00:21:45.250 --> 00:21:47.620
I'll kill you, noob!

00:21:47.620 --> 00:21:50.500
I-Itaru?

00:21:56.290 --> 00:22:01.330
Don't just let yourself in.
Can't you see I'm busy?

00:22:01.330 --> 00:22:04.830
Busy? You look like you're gaming.

00:22:04.830 --> 00:22:09.000
Wait... Who are you?

00:22:09.000 --> 00:22:12.200
Itaru Chigasaki.

00:22:12.200 --> 00:22:13.790
So what?
